cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Floodplain Reconnection Decision Tool in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Floodplain Reconnection Decision Tool"
type: software
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-11-20
repository-code: "https://github.com/USACE-WRISES/floodplain-reconnection"
url: "https://usace-wrises.github.io/floodplain-reconnection/"
abstract: "A web application that helps U.S. Army Corps of Engineers teams find, compare and choose floodplain reconnection projects. Its first step screens stream reaches from a national cross-section grid built on USGS 3DEP elevation data: bank height ratio and entrenchment ratio for every reach of about 1,000 ft, criteria the team sets, and a ranked shortlist of candidate sites."
authors:
  - family-names: Menichino
    given-names: Garrett T.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6719-6356"
    affiliation: "Environmental Laboratory, U.S. Army Engineer Research and Development Center"
keywords:
  - floodplain reconnection
  - site screening
  - bank height ratio
  - entrenchment ratio
  - stream restoration
  - Stream Tiered Assessment Framework
